    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 620,
      "text": "Start here\nThis Space is a small worked example: should a café open a second shop? Everything in it is invented, and you can delete it at any time.\n\n1. Select the market brief and choose “Open PDF”. It opens inside Knovum.\n\n2. Page 3 of the brief and the whiteboard photo are only pixels. Knovum reads them on this computer: select one and look for “Recognized text”. The first run downloads a small model.\n\n3. Connect a model in Settings and ask: “How long is the rent-free period, and when does the shop break even?” Each answer cites its source, and a citation leads to the page.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "sources",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 520,
